      "writtenOn": "2025-09-11T13:57:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This causes GPU to crash because we\u0027re asking to create new view regardless of the other cases in `RequiresCreatingNewTextureView`  where we returned `false`. I\u0027ve added logs as you can see, and creating a texture view with `R001` swizzle on `Depth16Unorm` is not allowed and makes GPU crash on macOS.\n\n```\nComputeMetalSwizzle() for texture format: TextureFormat::Depth16Unorm\nHasDepthOrStencil()\nswizzle: [ComponentSwizzle::R, ComponentSwizzle::Zero, ComponentSwizzle::Zero, ComponentSwizzle::One]\n[18518:12168639:0911/152041.772513:ERROR:gpu/command_buffer/service/dawn_context_provider.cc:111] Failed to create MTLTexture view.\n - While handling unexpected error type Internal when allowed errors are (Validation|DeviceLost).\n    at Initialize (../../third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/metal/TextureMTL.mm:884)\n    at Create (../../third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/metal/TextureMTL.mm:815)\n```\n\nI\u0027ve fixed the GPU crash by going back to this code (which I\u0027m not sure anymore is the right way) but CTS tests still fail.\n\n```\n    bool needsNewView \u003d RequiresCreatingNewTextureView(texture, GetInternalUsage(), descriptor,\n                                                       mtlSwizzle.has_value());\n```\n\nI can\u0027t figure out what is going on anymore... 😢",
      "revId": "17896857fef0d1f70b34f97f1ee34c67926fcd78",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70f775e9_6ee94698",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/metal/TextureMTL.mm",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 814,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-11T19:09:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It sounds like `RequiresCreatingNewTextureView` is misnamed. It checks both whether we *allow* creating a new texture view and whether we require it. It should be something like `ShouldCreateNewTextureView`. (Since evidently that method has somewhat complex logic, I think putting the `mtlSwizzle` check inside there makes sense, even though it\u0027s a trivial check.)\n\nI am guessing this is related to `RENDER_ATTACHMENT` and `STORAGE_BINDING` not allowing swizzles. Specifically one of these two [`return false;`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/metal/TextureMTL.mm;l\u003d134,148;drc\u003de095571be47008e6deca936cd0b8b45d1c937ca9) cases is probably no longer correct. I am not exactly sure why though.\n\nIf you run this with `--enable-backend-validation` (dawn) / `--enable-dawn-backend-validation` (chrome) hopefully you can get the Metal debug layer to tell you the exact error.",
      "parentUuid": "75ece351_ed836f23",
